# What the Vercel CLI must not upload. The CLI does not read .gitignore: it skips a short built-in
# list (.git, .next, .vercel, node_modules, .env.local, .env.*.local, .DS_Store) and whatever is
# listed here. Gitignore syntax, relative to this directory, which is where `vercel` runs from.
#
# The Vercel project builds apps/web. Besides that directory it needs the root package.json and
# package-lock.json, and a package.json for every workspace the lockfile names.

# Env files. The build takes its env from the Vercel project settings, never from a file.
.env
.env.*

# The iOS app
/apps/ios

# Backup copy of the Convex functions; the copy that deploys is apps/web/convex. It is an npm
# workspace (@enchatto/convex) in package-lock.json, so its package.json stays for npm install.
/apps/convex/*
!/apps/convex/package.json

# Stress-test output
/apps/web/scripts/stress-test-results-*.json

# tsc's incremental cache; next build keeps its own under .next
*.tsbuildinfo

# Repo tooling and docs
/.claude
/scripts
/deploy.sh
/*.md
